&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://asktia.com/company/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tia&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tia is building a new model for women’s healthcare, one that treats women as whole people, not separate conditions or life stages. By integrating primary care, mental health, gynecology, dermatology, and wellness across both in-person and virtual settings, Tia is improving outcomes, lowering costs, and creating a better experience for patients and providers alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;full-time &lt;/strong&gt;Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant to provide &lt;strong&gt;multi-site float coverage &lt;/strong&gt;across Tia’s Los Angeles clinics, including &lt;strong&gt;Pasadena, Silver Lake, Studio City, West Hollywood, Culver City, and Playa Vista.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll provide comprehensive primary care and women’s health services while supporting clinic coverage during staffing gaps, high-volume periods, PTO, training, or emergent needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for a clinician who brings strong outpatient primary care and women’s health experience, works well with autonomy, and can quickly integrate into different clinic teams while maintaining consistent care quality, workflow execution, and patient experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Tia&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to help shape and scale a new model of women’s healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-driven environment focused on improving care for women across life stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, thoughtful team committed to patient and provider experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern care model that integrates clinical care, operations, technology, and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful opportunity to support care delivery across multiple LA clinics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mileage reimbursement to and from clinic assignments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI documentation support to reduce administrative burden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to clinical education resources, including UpToDate and monthly internal training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Care:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide comprehensive primary care and women’s health services in an outpatient setting, including annual exams, pap smears, contraception counseling, STI screening, urgent care concerns, and whole-person care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Women’s Health &amp;amp; Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide gynecologic care, UTI and vaginal infection consults, and perform IUD insertions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Care Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage common primary care needs, including hypertension, diabetes, anxiety, depression, basic dermatologic concerns, cough, sore throat, abdominal pain, and related concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Site Coverage:&lt;/strong&gt; Float across Tia’s LA clinics to support staffing gaps, high-volume periods, training, PTO, and emergent coverage needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Quickly integrate into each clinic’s daily flow while upholding Tia’s standardized workflows, documentation expectations, and patient experience standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Care Model Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the ongoing iteration of Tia’s care model through technology development, interdisciplinary case studies, protocol development, clinical content review, and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Support:&lt;/strong&gt; When not in patient visits, support provider inbox work, RN team needs, clinical mentorship, or other care delivery priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;14esvje&quot; data-start=&quot;157&quot; data-end=&quot;173&quot;&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;175&quot; data-end=&quot;756&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1dy5ddu&quot; data-start=&quot;175&quot; data-end=&quot;310&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;177&quot; data-end=&quot;193&quot;&gt;Credentials:&lt;/strong&gt; NP or PA with national board certification, such as ANCC, AANP, or NCCPA; active California license; and active DEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;2jvprz&quot; data-start=&quot;311&quot; data-end=&quot;519&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;313&quot; data-end=&quot;336&quot;&gt;Clinical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of outpatient primary care experience with a focus on women’s health, including routine gynecology, contraception, STIs, mental health, and inclusive, patient-centered care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1y9v7oj&quot; data-start=&quot;520&quot; data-end=&quot;643&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;522&quot; data-end=&quot;544&quot;&gt;Technology &amp;amp; Data:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong comfort with technology, EHRs, AI-supported documentation, and data-informed care delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1w054gy&quot; data-start=&quot;644&quot; data-end=&quot;756&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;646&quot; data-end=&quot;666&quot;&gt;Float Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to work with high autonomy and adapt quickly across multiple clinic environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;gxq2rq&quot; data-start=&quot;758&quot; data-end=&quot;774&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;776&quot; data-end=&quot;1142&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1svo7i4&quot; data-start=&quot;776&quot; data-end=&quot;840&quot;&gt;Experience performing Nexplanon insertions and/or colposcopies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1mns7cq&quot; data-start=&quot;841&quot; data-end=&quot;917&quot;&gt;Experience in trauma-informed, LGBTQ+ inclusive, and gender-affirming care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;10zoz0i&quot; data-start=&quot;918&quot; data-end=&quot;989&quot;&gt;Experience managing depression and anxiety in outpatient primary care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;qaq4mj&quot; data-start=&quot;990&quot; data-end=&quot;1056&quot;&gt;Experience incorporating integrative medicine into care planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1sd6l1x&quot; data-start=&quot;1057&quot; data-end=&quot;1142&quot;&gt;Experience serving diverse communities across different care settings or modalities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in the &lt;strong&gt;Los Angeles market&lt;/strong&gt; and requires onsite coverage across multiple Tia clinics, including &lt;strong&gt;Pasadena, Silver Lake, Studio City, West Hollywood, Culver City, and Playa Vista&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Floats will primarily provide patient care at an assigned clinic for the day. Clinic assignments will be shared the night before or the morning of the shift. When not in patient visits, Floats may support provider inbox coverage, RN team needs, clinical content creation and review, clinical mentorship, or other care delivery priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tia is committed to pay equity and pay transparency. Compensation for this role will be determined based on job-related factors, including experience, skills, qualifications, location, role leveling, business needs, and market conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected compensation for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$140,000 - $170,000&lt;/strong&gt; annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also eligible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly performance bonus with a 10% target&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity grants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Malpractice coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off, sick leave, and holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CME stipend and licensing reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to clinical tools and ongoing training resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mileage reimbursement to and from clinic assignments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reimbursement for state licenses, board certification, and BLS certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DEA reimbursement where required for practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary subscription to UpToDate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal educational resources and monthly clinical training opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI documentation software designed to reduce clinical documentation burden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
