&lt;h2&gt;About Tia&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tia is building a new model for women’s healthcare that treats women as whole people rather than separate conditions or life stages. By integrating primary care, mental health, gynecology, dermatology, and wellness across in-person and virtual settings, Tia is improving outcomes and creating a better experience for patients and providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Part-Time Ultrasound Technologist (20 hours/week, with potential to increase over time)&lt;/strong&gt; to support Tia’s New York clinics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll perform high-quality gynecologic ultrasound exams, ensure accurate documentation and patient tracking, coordinate closely with providers and radiologists, and help create a compassionate, seamless experience for patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform high-quality gynecologic ultrasound exams with a strong focus on patient comfort and clinical excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review clinical indications and collaborate with ordering providers to ensure appropriate imaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate documentation and manage patient tracking and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit comprehensive studies to the radiologist and ensure results are returned to the ordering provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with providers and radiologists when additional review or escalation is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation to support clinical care and accurate billing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ultrasound workflows, including PACS, tele-radiology coordination, and equipment maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate patients as appropriate and contribute ultrasound expertise to Tia’s interdisciplinary care team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years of clinical ultrasound experience, including at least 1 year in OB/GYN, gynecology, or women’s health&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years of women’s health ultrasound experience preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent pelvic and gynecologic ultrasound scanning skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to recognize abnormalities and know when to escalate findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of gynecologic anatomy, symptoms, and common clinical indications for ultrasound&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PACS and radiology workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, organization, and patient follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication skills and comfort collaborating with providers and radiologists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compassionate, patient-centered approach to care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ultrasound documentation and billing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain and troubleshoot ultrasound equipment within scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Tia&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, mission-driven team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, vision, paid time off, paid sick leave, and paid learning time for teammates working 30+ hours per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical malpractice coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reimbursement for applicable state licenses, board certification, and BLS certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to UpToDate and extensive internal education and training resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-enabled documentation tools designed to reduce administrative burden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports &lt;strong&gt;Tia Williamsburg and Tia SoHo&lt;/strong&gt; and requires an onsite work schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected compensation range is &lt;strong&gt;$36–$48/hour&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tia is committed to pay equity and transparency. Compensation will be determined based on experience, skills, qualifications, location, role level, business needs, and market conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
