&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, interdisciplinary care team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training and clinical resources to help expand your knowledge of women’s health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive outpatient primary care, including preventive visits, health screenings, acute care, and chronic disease management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage common primary care concerns such as hypertension, diabetes, respiratory symptoms, digestive concerns, sleep issues, anxiety, depression, and basic dermatologic conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide evidence-based, patient-centered care using shared decision-making and a whole-person approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address common sexual and reproductive health needs within your experience and clinical scope, such as STI screening, urinary symptoms, contraception counseling, and menstrual concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize when patients need additional gynecologic evaluation, specialty referral, procedural care, or a higher level of care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review test results, develop treatment plans, communicate next steps, and coordinate follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with nurse practitioners, physicians, mental health clinicians, wellness providers, nurses, and clinic operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a collaborating physician for Tia’s New York nurse practitioners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support clinical teaching, coaching, and case consultation across the care team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Tia’s technology and product teams by providing clinical feedback on the tools used in patient care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on clinical research and incorporate evidence-based practices into day-to-day care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
